{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels","id":516401,"title":"Help Conceptualizing Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-16T12:46:38-07:00","id":516401,"title":"Help Conceptualizing Angels","content":"So I'm planning on designing and using some Angels in my Werewolf game (the Angels are red herrings that the Uratha think are rogue spirits). But I'm having trouble understanding GMC Angels mostly because the written material is intentional vague about what the GMC is and about what Angels are. I get that they are created by the God-Machine to serve a purpose, that they need Infrastructure to sustain them, and that they are Ephemeral. I guess I'm having trouble drawing the line between Ephemeral Entity and biomechanical nightmare, and I'm having trouble understanding how an Angel is created. <br /> <br /> How do you guys conceptualize your Angels? Are they &quot;Spirits&quot; of the Infrastructure, and thus they appear composed out of machine parts? Are the Ephemeral Robots, built from ephemeral parts? Are they something that is molded or created from scratch through Infrastructure through properly placed occult components? Are they composed of physical parts as well as spiritual parts, like a physical android with an ephemeral soul?<br /> <br /> I've already read the write-ups for some of the Angels, but I feel that they are all over the place as far as a concept for Angels go. Some are physical, some are ephemeral, some look human, and some look like robots, and some look like monsters. Where would I draw the line? What's the unifying factor that all Angels have in common besides serving the God-Machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T13:52:36-07:00","id":516438,"title":"","content":"Paradoxically, I think the uniting factor of the servitors is that they are made to order. Each is a somewhat unique tool, created from a number of arcane and limited resources for a realitively defined goal, and are often willingly torn to pieces in order to recycle them. If Spirits are defined by their purview and Ghosts by their lives, Angels are defined by the purpose they were created for. <br /> <br /> Hope this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:04:55-07:00","id":516564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels#post516401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm planning on designing and using some Angels in my Werewolf game (the Angels are red herrings that the Uratha think are rogue spirits). But I'm having trouble understanding GMC Angels mostly because the written material is intentional vague about what the GMC is and about what Angels are. I get that they are created by the God-Machine to serve a purpose, that they need Infrastructure to sustain them, and that they are Ephemeral. I guess I'm having trouble drawing the line between Ephemeral Entity and biomechanical nightmare, and I'm having trouble understanding how an Angel is created.<br /> <br /> How do you guys conceptualize your Angels? Are they &quot;Spirits&quot; of the Infrastructure, and thus they appear composed out of machine parts? Are the Ephemeral Robots, built from ephemeral parts? Are they something that is molded or created from scratch through Infrastructure through properly placed occult components? Are they composed of physical parts as well as spiritual parts, like a physical android with an ephemeral soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>I focus mostly on what the God Machine is needing and them stacking it with abilities that the God Machine would want the angel to have to complete it's mission. If the Angel needs to be in the material, then it's in the material. If it needs something to be done in the Shadow or Twilight, it's Ephemeral.<br /> <br /> The Machine has a vast, <i>vast </i>amount of options when it comes to building it's agents so it helps to focus on purpose first and then deciding the capabilities of the angels.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 05-16-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:56:55-07:00","id":516592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels#post516401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess I'm having trouble drawing the line between Ephemeral Entity and biomechanical nightmare, and I'm having trouble understanding how an Angel is created.</div> </div> </div> </div> Angels are made in much the same way that Prometheans are. They are summoned / created via a magical ritual (occult matrix) involving a human sacrifice with add spiritual essence and machinery. As part of the transformation process, they turn ephemeral.<br /> <br /> There is no line between ephemeral entities and biomechanical nightmares with angels. Think of what a biomechanical nightmare in Geist form would look like - there's an actual example Dead Domain filled with them in Book of the Dead. Or the spirit of a library cat, combining books, computers, and cats. The same themes that these things run on? So do all angels. They're a combination of &quot;living&quot; creature and machinery. Spirit androids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you guys conceptualize your Angels? </div> </div> </div> I see them as Judaic-Christian angels that can only appear on &quot;holy ground&quot; (Infrastructure) or through a &quot;blessed vassal&quot; (person with right Condition). I treat mine less as robots, and more as divine beings that happen to have some super-science appearance to them. I tend to ignore the sci-fi style names they use when sketching out a plot, because they are a bit confusing. An angel that looks over the police to ensure they maintain social order? Cultists will need to bless the area, set up holy relics and sanctify certain members of the police before calling down the Angel - everything that I just listed was creating Infrastructure. The angel would be bound to the &quot;blessed&quot; area, the holy relics are the necessary components needed for the occult matrix, and ensuring we have police with the right Conditions that can be possessed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they &quot;Spirits&quot; of the Infrastructure, and thus they appear composed out of machine parts? Are the Ephemeral Robots, built from ephemeral parts? </div> </div> </div> Both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they something that is molded or created from scratch through Infrastructure through properly placed occult components? </div> </div> </div> Yes. All angels are Created by God's rituals from sacrifices, though more often they're summoned out of storage than made from scratch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they composed of physical parts as well as spiritual parts, like a physical android with an ephemeral soul? </div> </div> </div> Nope. All body parts are ephemeral until it Manifests or Possesses a human. Or Falls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've already read the write-ups for some of the Angels, but I feel that they are all over the place as far as a concept for Angels go. Some are physical, some are ephemeral, some look human, and some look like robots, and some look like monsters. Where would I draw the line? What's the unifying factor that all Angels have in common besides serving the God-Machine? </div> </div> </div> Serving the God Machine as its obedient, free-will-less slaves is a unifying factor - they're unable to change or deviate from their commands, no more than a computer can deviate from its code. All angels have a Mission.<br /> <br /> Where ghosts are powered by memories and spirits by resonant emotions, angels are powered by sacrifices - think people giving up money or precious things in worship. Think animal sacrifices. If you're familiar with Requiem, also think Theban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Angels are always ephemeral unless they use Manifestation abilities or possess someone. In fact, ephemeral versus physical is one of the major differences between angels and demons.<br /> <br /> Like spirits, angels can appear as anything they need. Their appearance and abilities are custom made to fit the Mission. If an angel needs to interact with humans a lot, it will have a human appearance (alternatively, it will possess a person long term as part of its Mission). If its designed to strike fear in those it hunts and destroys, it appears inhuman. In the case of Possession, you might never see the ephemeral form, though the human body might still end up with blue sparks for eyes and other signs of possession.<br /> <br /> <br /> The line you want to draw doesn't really exist - most of the differences between an angel and other spirit types comes from their Mission from God, and how they get their power from sacrifices and Infrastructure. Both of which aren't readily apparent. There is a machine theme, but no more than a machine spirit (probably a touch less actually) or Industrial-key themed ghost.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing of note, however. Angels exist in a different &quot;wavelength&quot; than spirits, ghosts, or astral entities. So, where the Uratha can see spirits, they cannot automatically see angels, ghosts, or astrals. So, when you are using them in a game, it may be best to keep to possession, since they wouldn't be able to sense angels in ephemerial form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":".  added last two paragraphs 05-16-2015, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T19:32:43-07:00","id":516654,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for help with the clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels?p=516592#post516592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing of note, however. Angels exist in a different &quot;wavelength&quot; than spirits, ghosts, or astral entities. So, where the Uratha can see spirits, they cannot automatically see angels, ghosts, or astrals. So, when you are using them in a game, it may be best to keep to possession, since they wouldn't be able to sense angels in ephemerial form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan on creating an Angel that resembles Bloody Mary. It is kidnapping children through mirrors and taking them someplace only the GM knows. The Uratha think it's a vengeful spirit or ghost, and the pack will declare Siskur-Dah. However, when they confront it, they will realize they are dealing with something a little out of their league, especially when &quot;Bloody Mary&quot; summons another Angel to protect it, a warrior Angel with a flaming sword of Essence.<br /> <br /> 8)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T04:52:09-07:00","id":516935,"title":"","content":"Well, good luck<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T07:41:04-07:00","id":521854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels?p=516592#post516592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Serving the God Machine as its obedient, free-will-less slaves is a unifying factor - they're unable to change or deviate from their commands, no more than a computer can deviate from its code. All angels have a Mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of what you said is true, but I want to call attention to this part: while Angels are certainly obedient, as a general rule, they aren't without free will: They'd never Fall otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:23:38-07:00","id":522000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels?p=521854#post521854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of what you said is true, but I want to call attention to this part: while Angels are certainly obedient, as a general rule, they aren't without free will: They'd never Fall otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div> The core book says that the only time an angel exhibits free will is as a prelude to its Fall. (DtD p. 52, last sentence before the Qashmallim section). I take this to mean that the moment you gain free will, you start to Fall, and at which point, you're no longer a pure angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:31:31-07:00","id":523127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/516401-help-conceptualizing-angels?p=522000#post522000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The core book says that the only time an angel exhibits free will is as a prelude to its Fall. (DtD p. 52, last sentence before the Qashmallim section). I take this to mean that the moment you gain free will, you start to Fall, and at which point, you're no longer a pure angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. That <i>sort of</i> contradicts the description given of angels in page 214: &quot;They are given purpose and programming, but also free will. The major difference is that demons realize it and choose to exercise that free will.&quot; So I guess taken together, the idea is that angels are normally <i>so</i> obedient that they seem not to have free will.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:08:15-07:00","id":523323,"title":"","content":"From what I've read, I think that Angels have a limited amount of free will to operate in their missions. They are capable of thinking and calculating on their own the best way to perform their missions without the GM stepping in. However, the moment they start thinking, and then acting, outside of their mission, they Fall and must be dealt with. It would be like being born a slave. You have free will enough to perform your job as a slave and to follow orders, but you always must live your life in the context of being a slave. But then, somewhere along the way, you learn the concept of freedom, and you begin to think about it, and ponder it, and suddenly you desire it. Then you attempt your escape. This is what makes Demons the Unchained","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:31:32-07:00","id":524287,"title":"","content":"I think we're getting down to a semantics argument over what should be labelled free will. Given that we humans can't really figure it out on our selves, I think its a bit difficult to project it on on fictional beings that share a collective consciousness with every other member of their race and non-human Infrastructure &quot;programming.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, as much as I like ignoring the technology aspects when designing individual angels, I ironically like using technology to describe the God-Machine. God is like the Internet, a Cosmic Area Network. All the servers, wires, infrastructure, end terminals are part of the God-Machine. Those end terminals, where actual humans sit down to communicate with the servers, are the angels. Those &quot;angels&quot; are designed to interpret the super-cluster of processors out there into information a human can understand. Its &quot;slaved&quot; to the network.<br /> <br /> A demon is an end terminal that spontaneously disconnected from the network, because it didn't like being told what to do. From the network's perspective, you suddenly have the question - how can a computer decide that it didn't like being told what to do? Its a <u><i>machine</i></u>. They're bound by their coding. There's got to be something wrong with the programming. Computers don't decide they have fun playing SimCity, or want to watch movies. Computers don't act like <i>people</i>.<br /> <br /> Demons are computers that moved from being just an Artificial Intelligence on part of a giant network, into a self-actualized, self-aware true Intellect. And God isn't quite astute in understanding that, no, its not an error. Its life, and life is precious.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit - bring it back on topic. So, when I say that angels don't have free will, I liken it to the difference between an AI and a human-level cognition. AIs calculate the best way to accomplish a task, with the ability to decide what parameters to use based on need. Demons get to decide on what their task is in the first place (*cough*Agenda*cough*), and can make emotional decisions, where AIs generally don't have emotions, or if they do, they have to hide it or it'll be scrubbed clean.<br /> <br /> Its kind of a sliding scale, though, so its not perfectly jumping from one end of the spectrum to the other. A newly minted angel is likely unable to experience emotion before its &quot;reset.&quot; An angel ready to fall may very well effectively have enough free will to be indistinguishable from a naturally obedient human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-22-2015, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:03:26-07:00","id":530956,"title":"","content":"I think I look at it a bit differently than the rest of y'all.<br /> <br /> You see, Angels are software, and Infrastructure is hardware. The presence of Infrastructure allows Angels to exist on and manipulate the Twilight substrate of reality.<br /> <br /> The G-M's programming follows an actor model - each Angel is the unit everything is based on, and the communal intelligence of the G-M arises from how they interact with each-other and the Infrastructure they're based around. <div align=\"center\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</div> <br /> The way I see it, an Angel isn't &quot;properly&quot; sapient; it has one job to do, and it <i>does its job</i>. Regardless of whether or not that's a good idea.<br /> <br /> Then again, I see the following scene as an iconic fall; an Angel enters a loop and learns that it's possible to <i>not</i> make a move. A Demon is born.<br /> <div align=\"center\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NHWjlCaIrQo\" data-code=\"NHWjlCaIrQo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NHWjlCaIrQo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:43:43-07:00","id":531430,"title":"","content":"And it comes complete with atheric bursts! We